  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> aqueous solution will have lowest freezing point?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zhtSD",
      "text": "Potassium sulphate",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Fyuzj",
      "text": "Sodium chloride",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lr0le",
      "text": "Urea",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21MMO",
      "text": "Glucose",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Potassium sulphate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Sodium chloride <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>NaCl</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Urea, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Glucose, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Greater the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></math>, greater lowering in freezing point and hence, lower will be the freezing temperature.</p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> solution has the lowest freezing point.</p>",
